// Free, open data about the world, beyond single Wikidata items: a word's forms (Wikidata
// lexemes), the most or least of a kind (Wikidata's query service), money in another currency
// (Frankfurter, the European Central Bank's rates) and the weather (Open-Meteo). Each keeps where
// it came from. Written by scripts/pack.mjs from sources/world (edit those, not this).
Requires(Core(), Basic(), Code())

Concept(Frankfurter(), IsA(Source()), IsA(LearningSource()), License("European Central Bank reference rates"))

Concept(OpenMeteo(), IsA(Source()), IsA(LearningSource()), License("CC BY 4.0"))

Concept(Weather(), IsA(Result()))

// Being born, as Wikidata says it: when (date of birth, P569) and where (place of birth, P19),
// each by what it is called, so "i was born in 1990" and "when was i born" find them.
// What each takes, as Wikidata's datatype says (a time; an item, a place): which one a year or a
// city said after "born" is.
Concept(TakesValue(), IsA(Relation()))
Concept(DateOfBirth(), IsA(Relation()), SameAs(Wikidata("P569")), Called(Born()), Called(Birth(Date())), TakesValue(Date()))
Concept(PlaceOfBirth(), IsA(Relation()), SameAs(Wikidata("P19")), Called(Born(In())), Called(Birthplace()), TakesValue(Place()))
